# Issue #209 — real eval-report smoke run (lesson_hello)

## Invocation

Run from the worktree repo root (`/Users/carbonite/Documents/coding/portfolio/worktree-issue-209`),
branch `209-wholegame-evidence`, after `cargo run -p blendtutor-cli -- init target/hello-course`.

```bash
# FIREWORKS_API_KEY from environment (real key, present)
# PATH prefixed so run.sh can resolve both GNU `timeout` and the `blendtutor` binary
# (neither is on the default macOS PATH):
export PATH="$PWD/target/debug:/opt/homebrew/opt/coreutils/libexec/gnubin:$PATH"
FIREWORKS_API_KEY="$FIREWORKS_API_KEY" cargo run -p blendtutor-cli -- \
  eval-report "$PWD/target/hello-course/lesson_hello.yaml"
```

Lesson path passed ABSOLUTE (canonicalized at top of eval-report::run — AC-5
relative-arg ENOENT trap avoided). Report published by the command itself into
`docs/evals/lesson_hello/` (the command's `repo_root_for` resolves the repo via
the `.git` above the course and writes `<repo>/docs/evals/<lesson_id>/`).

