- `runs/case-2/.../output.txt` line 1: `verdict: incorrect`

Both match `^verdict: (correct|incorrect)$`. case-1 prompt `cat("hello\n")` →
expected `correct` (judge pass 0.96); case-2 prompt `cat("goodbye\n")` →
expected `incorrect` (judge fail 0.56).

## Environment notes (spec deviations — see summary.md)

1. Temp course initialized at `target/hello-course/` (inside the repo, gitignored
   via `/target`) instead of `/tmp/hello-course` — required by the implementation:
   `eval_report::run` resolves the report output dir via `repo_root_for()` (walks
   UP from the course for `.git`) and the runner script path via `scripts_rel_from()`
   (same walk). A /tmp course finds no `.git` ancestor → report cannot be
   published to `docs/evals/` and the runner path falls back to a broken
   `../../../../scripts/smevals/run.sh`. Anti-leak guarantees hold unchanged:
   `/target` + `**/.smevals/` gitignores + scoped `git add docs/evals/lesson_hello/`.
2. `timeout` (GNU coreutils) missing on macOS → `brew install coreutils`; PATH
   prefixed with `/opt/homebrew/opt/coreutils/libexec/gnubin`. No repo code changed.
3. `blendtutor` not on default PATH → PATH prefixed with `$PWD/target/debug`.
